	(footprint "Alps_SKTAAAE010_pads34"
		(layer "F.Cu")
		(uuid "609e1268-5e85-41ab-be20-c9cdcfde8bb0")
		(at 65.797373 77.5 -90)
		(descr "Alps Alpine SKTAAAE010 tact switch, 2.6 x 1.6 x 0.53 mm. Land pattern from the Alps Alpine SKTA series catalog design/datasheets/w4_alps_skta_catalog.pdf page 2, Drawing No.1: 'Land Dimensions' (outer span 3.2, inner span 2.1, overall height 1.3, gap 0.2: four lands 0.55 x 0.55 at +-1.325 and +-0.375 from the centre). Terminal numbers as Alps gives them in the 'Dimensions' view on the same page (seen from above): 1 top left, 2 top right, 3 bottom left, 4 bottom right; 'Circuit Diagram': terminals 1 and 3 are joined, 2 and 4 are joined, the contact is between the two pairs. Reflow profile: product specification slim_alps-skta-aaae010-orwin.pdf page 4 (peak 260 C max 3 s). Solder paste: an opening 1:1 (0.55 x 0.55) on every land of this footprint, layer F.Paste, for a 0.08 mm stencil (same page, item 10.2 (4); design/mfg/assembly/process.md sections P2 and P8 change C1). This variant has only lands 3 and 4 (bottom side): the head of the joystick tail is 6.4 mm wide and the outer lands 1 and 2 of the four outer switches would lie 0.15 mm from the cut edge (copper to edge needs 0.30, JLCPCB flexible PCB capabilities, row FPC Outline). Terminals 3 and 4 are the two ends of the contact, so the switch works with lands 3 and 4 alone; terminals 1 and 2 float (they are joined to 3 and 4 inside).")
		(tags "switch tact SKTA")
		(property "Reference" "SW3"
